  "research_id": "fsb-financial-system-transition-2009-2026",
  "title": "The FSB ties Basel, market infrastructure and digital finance together",
  "question": "How did the Financial Stability Board's post-crisis bank, resolution, clearing and non-bank programme become the international coordination spine for crypto, stablecoins, tokenisation, operational technology and implementation monitoring?",
  "bluf": "The FSB has spent fifteen years joining bank capital, failure, clearing, non-bank risk and implementation; crypto and tokenisation are the newest layer of that same system, not a separate global blockchain plan.",
  "evidence_cutoff": "2026-10-14",
  "evidence_cutoff_note": "Official FSB evidence through October 14, 2026. The regulatory and supervisory modernisation consultation and 2026 Implementation Monitoring Review are public. The IMR recommends written SRC/ReSG consultation with SCSI during drafting on monitorability while preserving Plenary decision authority; the consolidated framework remains to be drafted and approved. The modernisation principles remain proposed consultation text with comments due January 8, 2027 and national responsibilities retained.",
  "use_note": "Start with the whole-institution map, then use Wave 2 for banks, Wave 3 for derivatives/FMIs and the digital-finance map for crypto/DLT detail. Preserve BCBS/CPMI-IOSCO/FSB/national-authority roles; keep PFMI adoption, completeness, FMI outcomes, recovery and public resolution separate; do not promote a G20 request, FSB recommendation, consultation or peer review into binding law or operation.",
